WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.429
Aiko Tanabe:  Henrik, when you launched your first free channels in 2020, who did you think would watch them?

2
00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:00.857
Henrik Aalto:  Young people on smart TVs, honestly.

3
00:00:00.857 --> 00:00:01.286
Cord-cutters.

4
00:00:01.286 --> 00:00:01.714
What we got was very different: our biggest audience on the crime channels is over 55, watching in the afternoon.

5
00:00:01.714 --> 00:00:02.143
Aiko Tanabe:  Did that change how you programme them?

6
00:00:02.143 --> 00:00:02.571
Henrik Aalto:  Completely.

7
00:00:02.571 --> 00:00:03.000
We stopped repeating the same block every six hours.

8
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:03.429
We now have programmers who think about the afternoon like a linear channel would.

9
00:00:03.429 --> 00:00:03.857
Viewing time per session went up by a third.

10
00:00:03.857 --> 00:00:04.286
Aiko Tanabe:  And fill rates are at record highs.

11
00:00:04.286 --> 00:00:04.714
Is that the number you watch?

12
00:00:04.714 --> 00:00:05.143
Henrik Aalto:  It is the number I report, not the one I watch.

13
00:00:05.143 --> 00:00:05.571
A full ad break in front of nobody is still worth nothing.

14
00:00:05.571 --> 00:00:06.000
What I want is a way to count viewers that every platform accepts.
